#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/6df16dbe8d511d1e6aca8018bbb10acba27a6bca  (PR #2864)
# Author:    seedds, 2026-11-21 03:24:56 +0800
# Co-authors:
#   Co-authored-by: Oliver Ames
#   Co-authored-by: kenCalx
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); the attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES FOR THE PHONE
#   dm_gfx_suspend(1) used to wait, on the caller's thread, for the graphics calls in progress, the Vulkan / GL queues and mtl_drain() (all GPU work, the present queue, the snapshots),
#   then for the pipeline archive hand-over. A game in a long pipeline / library compile or a stalled GPU held that wait for ever, and iOS ends an app whose background callback does
#   not return (about 22 s). The app's call (app/patches/0030-suspend-graphics-in-background) runs it on the main thread in DidEnterBackground.
#   Now admission is closed at once (g_susp, mtl_set_present_suspended: present thread, display link and present_now take no frame), ONE worker owns the drain (gfx_drain_worker),
#   the caller waits at most 3 s and returns ("[RED] suspend: graphics did not drain in 3 s while waiting for <step>"), the archive hand-over runs on its own utility worker,
#   and dm_gfx_suspend(0) reopens graphics only when the drain is over and the app is in the foreground. Default: on, no switch.
#
# HAND-MERGED: upstream's display-link callback, present_main and present_drop_for_suspend differ from this tree's (frame generation 0205, g_present_suspended, latch 0206): five hunks
#   redone by hand with the same logic (no frame while g_present_suspended, g_link_presenting counted around the callback's present, present_suspend_wait(), drop_queued_presents_locked()).
#   snap_drain() of the frame-generation teardown became snap_drain(1). nvn_queue_present_wait takes the one-line `physical || copy`.
#   ADDED (not upstream): one line in hle_nvn.c keeps a reference to mtl_drain (no caller left): without it the SIMULATOR host would stop exporting _mtl_drain and build-host.sh's
#   "no export lost" check would fail. LEFT OUT: dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m (the engine's own shell, not linked in GameApp) and the docs.
#
# RISK: medium (lifecycle gate and present hand-off). Look for "[nvn] graphics suspended" / "resumed" in gameapp.guest.log after Home. NOT run on a device. Shader chain id untouched.
#
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0415, in the order of the numbers of this folder.

